//
// Fire risk assessment, fire safety checks, evacuation readiness, window
// restrictors, hot water and hot surfaces, legionella, hazardous substances,
// lifting equipment (LOLER), night working, oxygen storage, electrical and gas.
//
// Each check is a list of questions whose failing answers carry a severity
// and the action to take. Critical: someone could be badly hurt or killed —
// act today. Major: a legal or guidance requirement is not met — act this
// week. Minor: improve. The evacuation check also reads the home's PEEPs, so
// "do we have enough night staff and equipment for the people who need it?"
// is answered from the residents' own plans, not guessed.
//
// These checks support, and never replace, the competent-person assessments
// the law requires (fire risk assessment, legionella risk assessment, LOLER
// thorough examinations, electrical and gas inspections). Pure; tested in
// backend/tests/homesafety.test.mjs.
